AB  - Image captioning methods, particularly based on Multimodal Large Language Models (MLLMs), often generate hallucinatory descriptions. While existing methods primarily address this issue from the spatial domain, they often overlook the influence of frequency-domain features on the language generation stage. In this paper, we study the cause of hallucinations from frequency domain and attribute them to the model’s susceptibility to the frequency perturbations, which manifesting as the generation of hallucinations with high uncertainty. Based on this finding, we introduce frequency perturbations into models to reduce sensitivity and propose a novel plug-and-play metric Frequency Perturbation Entropy (FPE) to reduce the language generation uncertainty when conditioned on these perturbations, thereby mitigating hallucinations. Specifically, we derive the variational FPE to establish an FPE loss that guides the model to predict text with high certainty, which is implemented through a perturbation modeler and a text generator. The experimental results demonstrate that our proposed FPE can not only mitigate hallucinations, but also help the baseline models obtain obvious performance gains. Source code is available at https://github.com/Panlizhi/FPE.
