AB  - This chapter presents an in-depth exploration of the current challenges faced by machine learning-based cyber-attack detection in IoT networks. Key issues such as the sparsity of attack vectors, the heterogeneity of IoT devices, the need for real-time processing, and privacy concerns are thoroughly examined through specific use cases and scenarios. The chapter then explores innovative research directions and solutions, including adversarial training, transfer learning, and federated learning, as well as novel model designs tailored for IoT environments, such as advanced compression and quantization techniques. Finally, emerging trends such as privacy-preserving machine learning, tiny AI, large language models (LLMs), and quantum computing are discussed as promising avenues for enhancing cyber-attack detection in IoT networks.
